# TF2's mini-crit text up close (specs/tf2/batch2b_mechanics.md 18): the
# Cleaner's Carbine's crikey filled at a target 3 m away, attack2, then
# one bullet (`minicrit_text`) and a stream of them (`minicrit_stream`,
# 12 frames after its first hit past 0.3 s; game-time waits, so a
# slow frame rate fires no more): each must show one crisp
# yellow text (a stream's once piled up as several jittered copies, each
# hit's at its own size). Needs the item pack.
#   CHIMERA_ASSET_STORE=<store> cargo run --features dev --bin ultimate_gun_game -- --offscreen 1600x900 +volume 0 +sandbox \
#       --scene apps/ultimate_gun_game/scenes/tf2_crikey_close.scene --out <dir>
wait_for map_loaded 6000
wait_for spawned 3000
wait 120
god
sandbox ammo on
rung tf2:cleaners_carbine
target add tf2:tf_weapon_minigun 3
wait 2
wait_for idle 3000
wait 120
target look 1
+attack
gwait 1.2
-attack
wait 10
+attack2
wait 5
-attack2
wait 20
target look 1
shot_after hit 12 minicrit_text
+attack
wait 1
-attack
wait 60
+attack
gwait 0.3
shot_after hit 12 minicrit_stream
gwait 0.3
-attack
wait 30
